<title>USA: Texas/w Okla fed cattle market inactive - USDA.</title>
<headline>Texas/w Okla fed cattle market inactive - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>AMARILLO 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was inactive in the Panhandle area early Monday, USDA said.</p>
<p>Slaughter steers and heifers not tested. Feedlots reporting moderate inquiry from buyers. The last established price was $68.00-$69.00 per cwt on Friday. Monday's packer bids were $68.00, with asking prices $70.00-$71.00.</p>
<p>Note - all cattle prices based on net weights FOB the feedlot after a 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>Confirmed - None</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
